  "chatter": "<p>Iowa has trended redder in recent election cycles, and backed President Trump in all three of his campaigns. But now Trump’s unpopularity means Iowa Republicans are facing headwinds.\n<br><br>\nEven though the state’s entire congressional delegation is Republican and only one Democrat holds statewide office — state Auditor Rob Sand, who’s running for governor — Democrats are hopeful in Iowa this year.\n<br><br>\nThe U.S. Senate and governor’s races are seen as competitive, as are three of its four U.S. House<span class=\"widont\">&nbsp;</span>contests.</p>\n"
